<title>UK: Iran tells OPEC it pumped 3.594 mbpd in December.</title>
<headline>Iran tells OPEC it pumped 3.594 mbpd in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran told OPEC it produced  3.594 million barrels per day (bpd) in December, the OPEC News Agency OPECNA said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Iran has an OPEC quota of 3.6 million bpd.</p>
<p>A Reuter survey of officials, industry monitors and analysts put the country's December wellhead output at 3.7 million bpd, 20,000 bpd down from the November estimate.</p>
<p>OPEC sets its quota according to supply to the market and not by wellhead output. Supply as defined by OPEC is calculated as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products plys withdrawls of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>December production and supply data received so far by the OPEC Secretariat is as follows (in 1,000 bpd):</p>
<p>COUNTRY	  PRODUCTION	SUPPLY     QUOTA</p>
<p>-------	  ----------	------     -----</p>
<p>ALGERIA	   793.0	     760.0	750.0</p>
<p>INDONESIA     1,326.9	   1,326.6    1,330.0</p>
<p>IRAN	    3,594.0	   3,594.0    3,600.0</p>
<p>KUWAIT	  2,003.1	     N.A.     2,000.0</p>
<p>LIBYA	   1,398.0	   1,397.0    1,390.0</p>
<p>QATAR	     394.1	     381.7	378.0</p>
<p>SAUDI ARABIA  8,008.1	   7,989.3    8,000.0</p>
<p>UAE	     2,162.2	   2,180.0    2,161.0</p>
<p>VENEZUELA     2,391.0	   2,381.0    2,359.0</p>
<p>(N.A. - NOT AVAILABLE )</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7629</p>
